EXT. RIVER OF ASH - FERRY - TWILIGHT

A black skiff drifts on slow grey water. Pale ash falls like snow.

IXARA, 30s, ferrywoman, silver-white hair, poles in silence. BRUM, 50s, a traveler in a cloak, sits upright with a lantern at his feet.

IXARA
Where to?

BRUM
The far shore.

IXARA
Everyone says the far shore.

BRUM
Everyone's headed there.

IXARA
Not everyone has the fare.

BRUM
I have the fare.

IXARA
What is it?

BRUM
A name.

IXARA
Whose?

BRUM
Yours.

IXARA
(carefully)
Mine's not for sale.

BRUM
It's not for sale. It's for the toll. You told it to the last passenger, and he told it to me. You have been Ixara for nine hundred years. Before that you were someone else.

IXARA
Hush.

BRUM
They had a name for you in the old tongue. I have it here.

IXARA
Stop.

IXARA
(together)
Do not speak it.

BRUM^
I'm going to speak it.

Ash thickens. The lantern gutters.
